# civil-holidays v1
# jurisdiction: ID
# source: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Public_holidays_in_Indonesia
#   (the annual SKB three-minister decree of "Hari Libur Nasional").
#   Cross-checked against vacanza/holidays 0.101 (MIT). Names are the official
#   Indonesian.
#
#   MAXIMAL MULTI-RELIGIOUS MIX — four calendars in one jurisdiction:
#     * Islamic (islamic_civil, tabulated): Isra Mikraj, Idul Fitri, Idul Adha,
#       Tahun Baru Islam, Maulid — arithmetic Hijri, ±1-2 days from the decreed
#       sighting dates (catalogued in the differential test).
#     * Balinese Saka (Nyepi) and Buddhist (Waisak) and Chinese (Imlek): these
#       lunar/lunisolar calendars are not in the engine's registry, so they are
#       decree rows carrying the SKB-gazetted dates (honest tabulation).
#     * Christian (Gregorian Easter): Wafat Yesus Kristus (Good Friday),
#       Kebangkitan (Easter Sunday, a national holiday only from 2024),
#       Kenaikan (Ascension) — exact Easter offsets.
#   The two 2024 electoral holidays (Pemilihan Umum / Kepala Daerah) are
#   one-off decree dates.
# retrieved: 2026-07-22
# categories: public|regional|municipal|religious|school
# columns: kind | name | args | categories | subdiv | observed | valid | span
#
# --- fixed civil ---
fixed | Tahun Baru Masehi                        | 1 1   | public          |  |
fixed | Hari Buruh Internasional                 | 5 1   | public          |  |
fixed | Hari Lahir Pancasila                     | 6 1   | public          |  |
fixed | Hari Kemerdekaan Republik Indonesia      | 8 17  | public          |  |
fixed | Hari Raya Natal                          | 12 25 | public religious |  |
#
# --- Christian (Gregorian Easter offsets) ---
easter | Wafat Yesus Kristus       | -2 | public religious |  |
easter | Kebangkitan Yesus Kristus | 0  | public religious |  |  | 2024-
easter | Kenaikan Yesus Kristus    | 39 | public religious |  |
